```
# ============================================================================
# Detection: Command-Line Search for Stored Credentials
# Detection ID: DE-CA-002
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1552.001 - Unsecured Credentials: Credentials In Files
# Data Source: Sysmon EventCode=1
# Severity: Medium
# ============================================================================

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=1
Image IN ("*\\findstr.exe","*\\cmd.exe","*\\powershell.exe")
CommandLine="*password*" OR CommandLine="*credential*" OR CommandLine="*.kdbx*" OR CommandLine="*unattend.xml*"
| stats count min(_time) as first_seen values(CommandLine) as cmd by ComputerName, User, Image
| eval first_seen=strftime(first_seen,"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
| sort -count
```

## Detection Logic
Attackers routinely grep the filesystem (findstr /si password *.txt *.xml *.config) for stored credentials in configs, scripts, and legacy unattend.xml files after gaining initial foothold.

## False Positive Considerations
Developers/helpdesk staff occasionally run similar searches for legitimate troubleshooting — treat as medium-severity triage item, not auto-page.

## Tuning Notes
Extend CommandLine matching to include 'connectionstring', 'apikey', 'secret' for broader DevSecOps coverage.
